## Question

Which Typed supervision contract does goPekko adopt (default Stop, `supervise`/`onFailure`, Resume, Restart, restart limits, backoff,
stash during restart, stopping children, `PreRestart`/`PostStop`/`ChildFailed`, failures in setup, processing and message
adaptation), selected per actor at creation (ADR 0033 D2), on the shared runtime and without changing the Classic profile of ADR 0017?
Waiting for the answer: #956 (TYP-09), #1183, #1184, #994 (Typed System guardian), and every Typed story that restarts or stashes.

## The finding that shapes the answer: who applies the default Stop

"Classic restarts, Typed stops" is true of the **outcome** but hides two different **mechanisms**, chosen by how the Typed actor was
spawned (`AA/ActorContextAdapter.scala:69, 74`; `T/scaladsl/adapter/package.scala:56-130`):

| Spawned by | Mechanism | Parent observes |
|---|---|---|
| A Typed actor (`ctx.spawn`) | No wrapper. The failure escapes the child; the **parent's** adapter strategy returns Stop for a Typed child (`AA/ActorAdapter.scala:232-262`: `TypedActorFailedException` at 236-239, `isTypedActor` defined at 241-246 and tested at 258, Stop at 258-259) | `ChildFailed(ref, cause)` if it watches the child, else nothing |
| A Classic actor, a Classic System, `systemActorOf` or `PropsAdapter` | The behavior is wrapped in `supervise(_).onFailure(stop)`; the **child** stops itself; the Classic parent's strategy is not consulted (the wrapper is built at `AA/ActorSystemAdapter.scala:130` and `T/scaladsl/adapter/PropsAdapter.scala:34`, and for the Classic system and context `spawn`/`spawnAnonymous` at `T/scaladsl/adapter/package.scala:60, 74, 114, 127`; its failure ends in `context.stop(self)` at `AA/ActorAdapter.scala:168-172`), **except** when the user's own match-all `supervise` replaces that wrapper (matrix, decision-3 row) | plain `Terminated` |
| A Typed actor, child is Classic | The parent adapter's decider `defaultDecider.applyOrElse(_, Restart)` (`AA/ActorAdapter.scala:55-58, 261`; `A/FaultHandling.scala:218-223`): Stop on `ActorInitializationException`, `ActorKilledException` and `DeathPactException`; every other non-fatal failure, a non-fatal `Error` included, is Restart (a Classic parent would escalate an `Error`) | `ChildFailed` if watched and stopped |

So a Classic parent with the default Restart strategy and an unsupervised Typed child gets a **stopped** child
(`TT/coexistence/ClassicSupervisingTypedSpec.scala:105`), and a Typed parent with an unsupervised Classic child gets a **restarted**
child for an `Exception` (`TT/coexistence/TypedSupervisingClassicSpec.scala:61-71`; a non-fatal `Error` restarts too, CODE).

