**Proposed precision of ADR 0033 D2 (wording for the Owner; not an approval of it):**

> Classic and Typed coexist as two profiles on the shared runtime. The profile of an actor is fixed when it is created, by the API that
> creates it: an actor created by `pekko-actor-typed` from a `Behavior[T]` has the Typed profile; every other actor has the Classic
> profile. A Typed actor that has no matching `supervise` stops on failure whoever its parent is. When its parent is a Typed actor, the
> parent's Typed strategy applies the stop and the parent may observe `ChildFailed`; otherwise the actor's own default stop applies it
> and the parent observes `Terminated`. A Classic child keeps the Classic defaults of ADR 0017, including under a Typed parent; there it is decided by Pekko's adapter
> decider (initialization, kill and death-pact errors stop; other non-fatal failures restart). Nothing in
> the Typed profile changes the behavior of a Classic actor.

