stopping children, then backoff and stash once a timer source and the event stream exist). Slicing is a delivery plan, not a pending
contract, which is why (c) is not recommended.

**Owner decision: S-1 and S-6 accepted on 2026-10-27 (status line); S-2 to S-5 pending.** The questions are now decisions S-1 to S-6 of `docs/parity/typed-supervision-decision-package-2026-10-27.md`; they supersede readiness
decisions 2 to 4 and the list below, kept for the record. D-b and D-d are Pekko behavior; contract 8, D-a, D-f, the cause of contract 14
and the M-B case are decided separately.
